  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be non-collinear vectors. If <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is a vector such that <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>.</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, then <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the line",
